From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Poyu Chen <me@poyu.xyz>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 06:01:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci_sync: use controllers that refuse LE commands
 as BR/EDR only

The TI WL1283 advertises LE in its LMP features, but with its init script
(TIInit_10.6.15.bts) it answers LE Read Supported States with Command
Disallowed, which aborts the whole controller initialisation. When a
dual-mode controller refuses LE commands this way, clear the LE feature
bit and continue as a BR/EDR-only controller.

Upstream: not submitted
---
 net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c b/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
index f79b38603..8504c458a 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
@@ -4039,8 +4039,21 @@ static int hci_init2_sync(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 
 	if (lmp_le_capable(hdev)) {
 		err = hci_init_stage_sync(hdev, le_init2);
+		/* Some dual-mode controllers advertise LE in their LMP features
+		 * but refuse LE commands with "Command Disallowed" (for example
+		 * the TI WL1283 with an init script that has no LE support).
+		 * Use them as BR/EDR-only controllers instead of failing the
+		 * whole initialisation.
+		 */
+		if (err == -EBUSY && lmp_bredr_capable(hdev)) {
+			bt_dev_warn(hdev, "LE commands disallowed; using the controller as BR/EDR only");
+			hdev->features[0][4] &= ~LMP_LE;
+			err = 0;
+		}
 		if (err)
 			return err;
+		if (!lmp_le_capable(hdev))
+			return 0;
 		/* LE-only controllers have LE implicitly enabled */
 		if (!lmp_bredr_capable(hdev))
 			hci_dev_set_flag(hdev, HCI_LE_ENABLED);
